    "He understood that The Best Ideas in Business Always Come from the Frontline Workers Who Touch the Customer Every Day, not from detached executives sitting in corporate boardrooms. He listened to cashiers, truck drivers, and shelf-stockers, empowering them to experiment with localized merchandising.",
